- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`

**How to implement.** The kit's naming template is shown and saved in the kit bar, through semantic messages (001 §J 'Naming template: each kit carries one'; 001 §P and .spec-md §4 'UI': every user step is a semantic message, and the button and the test send the same one; S12.1 builds its kit with the lab's template). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `type Kit.NamingTemplate with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, the template's text, with a one-line doc. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, in the kit bar group (step 188), each with a one-line doc: `namingTemplateField` (`"NamingTemplateField"`) and `saveNamingTemplateButton` (`"SaveNamingTemplateButton"`). (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) The model gains `namingTemplateText : ControlCaption`, the template being typed, with a one-line doc; it is the kit file's `namingTemplate.caption` wherever the model takes a kit file: `initWith`, the open's `loadKit` and `ReloadKitChanges` (step 187), so a reload shows a template another writer saved. (b) Messages, each with a one-line doc: `SetNamingTemplateText of ControlCaption` (the field's text) and `SaveNamingTemplate` (the kit's naming template becomes the field's). (c) Arms. `SetNamingTemplateText text` sets `namingTemplateText`. `SaveNamingTemplate` is refused by the read-only guard of step 185, as `SaveSetup` is (step 262). Otherwise `NamingTemplate.tryCreate model.namingTemplateText.value` (step 268): `Error e` sets `kitStatus` to `Not saved — <e.describe>` and writes nothing; a template equal to `model.kit.kitFile.namingTemplate` sets `The naming template is unchanged.` and writes nothing; any other is written by `model.kit.saveKitFile { model.kit.kitFile with namingTemplate = template }` (step 131), whose `Ok kit` makes `model.kit` that context and `kitStatus` `Saved the naming template.`, and whose `Error e` keeps the model and sets `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. The window's own write is not a change offered for reload (step 130), and no setup or experiment is renamed (step 271). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs` (step 188): after the Kit menu's `WrapPanel` (step 188 (2)(b)), a `DockPanel` whose left child is the semi-bold `TextBlock` `Naming template:`, whose right child is the `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` `Save template` carrying `saveNamingTemplateButton` and sending `SaveNamingTemplate`, present only while the kit's writes are offered (`model.kitWrites`, step 185), and whose fill is a `TextBox` carrying `namingTemplateField` that shows `namingTemplateText` and sends `SetNamingTemplateText` at every change of its text. No other message, field, id or option is added. Tests. `KitWindowModelTests` (steps 184-187), over a folder kit: `Save template writes the typed naming template into the kit file`: `SetNamingTemplateText (ControlCaption "{source:CPL1=CPL}-({obj1}#{phi1})-{analyzer:CPL2=CPL}")` and `SaveNamingTemplate` leave that template in `model.kit.kitFile.namingTemplate`, `model.kit.proxy.readKitFile ()` answers a kit file holding it, `kitStatus` is `Saved the naming template.` and `CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnRequest` offers no change. `a naming template that does not parse, or the kit's own, is told and writes nothing`: the text `{sauce}` sets a `kitStatus` starting `Not saved` and holding `the naming template is not valid`, and the standard text sets `The naming template is unchanged.`; the bytes of `.kit-json` are unchanged by both. `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` (step 185) also sends `SaveNamingTemplate` after a template is typed, with the same assertions. `Reload reads the kit's files in and clears the offer` (step 187) also has the other writer save a kit file whose template is `{obj1}`, and after Reload `namingTemplateText` is `{obj1}`. `KitWindowTests` (step 188): `the kit bar shows the kit's naming template with Save template beside it`: `namingTemplateField` shows the kit's template text, `saveNamingTemplateButton` is present with its left beyond the field's right, and the ids' texts are `NamingTemplateField` and `SaveNamingTemplateButton`; `a read-only window withholds every write control` (step 185) also finds no `saveNamingTemplateButton`. `ScrollExtentTests`' kit-window fact passes unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the template is edited in the kit bar, `SetNamingTemplateText` and `SaveNamingTemplate` MUST set and save the kit's naming template through `KitContext.saveKitFile`, refusing a text that does not parse, an unchanged template and a read-only kit with nothing written, and the kit bar MUST show the template's field and Save template; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `Save template writes the typed naming template into the kit file` and `a naming template that does not parse, or the kit's own, is told and writes nothing` and the changed `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` and `Reload reads the kit's files in and clears the offer`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the kit bar shows the kit's naming template with Save template beside it` and the changed `a read-only window withholds every write control`; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.
